@* Enroll a student in a grade level. The dialog is a thin shell over
   StudentsApiClient.EnrollStudentAsync; it presents the canonical
   school-collab FormRow form (period, grade, enrolled-on date) and
   the shared DialogShellFooter handles save/cancel/error/saving
   state. Each field is wrapped in the shared <FormRow> primitive so
   the labels are equal-width (180px) and every input's left edge
   lands on the same vertical axis — matches the repo-wide form
   layout convention (v4.14.2; see FormRow.razor for the full pattern).
   The dialog intentionally does NOT render a "Student" row — the
   caller (Detail.razor / Edit.razor) already shows the student
   context on the page, and re-stating it inside the dialog is
   redundant (the user just clicked "Enroll" on a specific student's
   page; they know which student they're enrolling).

   The period is NOT a user-pickable dropdown. Enrollments are
   always against the tenant's CURRENT GLOBAL PERIOD (the single
   <PeriodStatus.Active> period for the current tenant; derived
   client-side by listing periods and filtering by Status == "Active",
   the same approach <ActiveTermToolbar> uses for the toolbar).
   The server enforces this too: <EnrollStudentHandler> resolves
   <IActivePeriodProvider.GetActivePeriodAsync()> and throws
   <PeriodNotOpenException> if the request's PeriodId does not match
   the active one. We surface the active period as a read-only
   "Period" row in the form so the user can see what the enrollment
   is going against, and submit with that period's id. There is no
   period dropdown because there is no choice to make — the only
   valid enrollment period is the active one, the server will reject
   anything else, and giving the user a picker would let them pick
   a value the server is going to reject.

   The active period is shown in the canonical academic-year format
   "<StartDate.Year>/<EndDate.Year>" (e.g. "2025/2026"). This is
   the standard school-collab display: short enough to fit in a
   single line of the read-only input cell regardless of the period
   name, and the full name + date range is exposed as a native
   <code>title=</code> tooltip on the input so the user can hover
   for the complete context without the row overflowing the form.

   The grade is picked via the shared <CodedValueDropdown
   Parent="CodedValueParent.Grades">, which loads the
   tenant-resolved CodedValue list from the Settings service and
   shows the per-tenant override name (e.g. "Year 7" instead of
   the default "Grade 7"). The same widget is used by the
   GradeLevelWizard step 1 and the student form's gender field.
   The dropdown does NOT load the GradeLevelDto stale mirror;
   it loads the live CodedValueDto so a tenant override shows up
   The submit travels as the selected CodedValueId; the server joins it to
   the GradeLevel row (materializing one if missing) at enroll time.

   A "+" button next to the grade dropdown lets the user create a
   brand-new grade level inline. The flow:
     1. Click the + button next to "Grade level".
     2. The shared <CodedValueDialog> opens in Create mode for the
        GRADE parent — collects a code, name, and display order.
        The Name field is the per-tenant override name; the user
        can leave it empty to use the code as the display name, or
        enter a tenant-specific label (e.g. "Year 7" instead of
        "Grade 7" for a school that uses a different vocabulary).
     3. On success we refresh the CodedValueDropdown (via its
        RefreshAsync) and pre-select the new coded value. Its
        GradeLevel row materializes server-side when the enrollment
        is submitted. The user is left on the same form with a
        working selection and clicks Enroll.
     4. If the user cancels the create dialog, we do nothing — the
        existing selection is preserved.
   This avoids the round-trip out of the dialog to the wizard /
   grade levels page just to add a grade, which was the friction
   point.

   The "+" button is GATED by TWO things, ANDed together:
     - The runtime feature flag FEATURE:EnableGradeLevelSetupOnEnrollDialog
       (opt-in, default false). The flag exists because the inline-
       create-grade action has a global side-effect: it creates a new
       GRADE coded value and a matching GradeLevel row, both of
       which are shared across tenants. Toggling the flag on via
       the ConfigFlags landing page exposes the "+" button
       reactively (the FeatureFlagGate re-evaluates on the
       IFeatureFlagChangeNotifier event) — no page reload required.
     - The new-enrollment check <see cref="IsNewEnrollment"/>. The
       "+" button only renders for a NEW enrollment (the student
       has no active enrollment yet, signalled by
       <EnrollStudentModel.SuggestedGradeLevelId> being null — the
       call sites pass the student's current active-enrollment
       grade as that field). For a re-enrollment the button is
       hidden: the user is "moving an already-enrolled student",
       and adding a brand-new grade mid-flow is the wrong action
       (a re-enrollment is supposed to pick a different existing
       grade, not stand one up). The check is the validation that
       "setting up a grade level inside the enrollment dialog" is
       a valid action for the current scenario.

   The "Enrolled on" field has a per-field error display
   (<FluentMessageBar Intent="Error">) rendered DIRECTLY BELOW the
   date picker. The dialog's submit failure error (set on the
   <Error> property by <SubmitAsync> on the null-return or
   throw path) is surfaced in TWO places:
     1. Right below the "Enrolled on" field — so the error is
        visually associated with the field that caused it (a
        rejected enrollment is almost always a date / grade /
        period issue, and the date is the most user-edited field
        on this form). This is the primary user-facing display.
     2. In the shared <DialogShellFooter> at the bottom of the
        dialog — kept for symmetry with every other
        <DialogShellBase> dialog and so the error survives a
        scroll-to-bottom by a user who missed the in-context
        message. The footer copy is the same text.
   A future "per-grade error" / "per-period error" variant is
   possible if the dialog grows a field-specific failure path;
   the current single-error-display model is sufficient for the
   happy path and the small set of API failures (open-period,
   grade-deleted, etc.) the server surfaces.

   The dialog does NOT special-case the empty-grade list. There is
   no "no grades available" blocking warning, no setup CTA inside
   the form, and no Disabled/Placeholder on the grade dropdown. A
   tenant with zero grade levels sees a populated-but-empty
   dropdown (the Enroll submit will be client-side disabled by
   the EditForm because no grade is selected, and the server's
   EnrollStudentAsync is the source of truth for grade validity).
   The setup-grade flow is the user's responsibility — they
   either flip the flag on to reveal the "+" button inline (for
   the new-enrollment case) or use the wizard / grade-levels
   landing page directly. The rationale for dropping the
   empty-list check: the dialog's job is to collect a well-formed
   enrollment; whether the tenant has any grade levels at all is
   a configuration concern that lives outside this dialog, and
   the server-side validation is the final authority on whether
   the chosen grade is valid. Forcing the user to bounce out of
   the dialog to fix a config gap was higher friction than the
   warning was worth. *@
@inherits DialogShellBase<EnrollStudentModel, EnrollStudentResult>
@using SchoolCollab.Students.Application.Services
@using SchoolCollab.Admin.Shared.Components
@using SchoolCollab.Admin.Shared.Constants
@using SchoolCollab.Admin.Shared.Services
@using SchoolCollab.Core.Features
@using Microsoft.FluentUI.AspNetCore.Components
@inject StudentsApiClient Api
@inject CodedValuesApiClient CodedValuesApi
@inject IDialogService DialogService
@inject ILogger<EnrollStudentDialog> Logger

<div class="enroll-dialog">
    @if (_loading)
    {
        <FluentProgressRing />
    }
    else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Error))
    {
        <FluentMessageBar Intent="MessageIntent.Error">@Error</FluentMessageBar>
    }
    else if (_activePeriod is null)
    {
        @* No active period. The server's <EnrollStudentHandler> rejects
           any enrollment whose PeriodId does not match the tenant's
           active period, so this is a hard block. Surface a clear
           action: open a period first. *@
        <FluentMessageBar Intent="MessageIntent.Warning">
            No active academic period is open for this tenant. Open a period on the
            <FluentAnchor Href="/students/periods" Appearance="Appearance.Hypertext">periods</FluentAnchor>
            page before enrolling.
        </FluentMessageBar>
    }
    else
    {
        @* The form follows the canonical school-collab FormRow layout:
           each field is a horizontal row with a fixed-width 180px label
           on the left and a flex-1 input cell on the right. The
           grade row composes a <CodedValueDropdown> (left) with a
           "+" inline-create-grade button (right) inside a single
           input cell. *@
        <EditForm Model="_formModel" OnValidSubmit="HandleSubmitAsync">
            <FluentStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Spacing="3">
                <FormRow Label="Period">
                    @* The period is the tenant's CURRENT GLOBAL period
                       (Status == "Active"). It is read-only — the
                       server's <EnrollStudentHandler> enforces the
                       active period, so the user has no choice to make.
                       The row is rendered as a FormRow (not a free
                       <div>) so its label "Period" lines up with the
                       other fields' labels down the form.

                       The display is the canonical academic-year
                       format "{StartDate.Year}/{EndDate.Year}"
                       (e.g. "2025/2026") so the read-only input cell
                       always fits the full text on one line regardless
                       of the period's name (e.g. "Fall 2025 / Spring
                       2026" is much longer than the 9-char academic-
                       year token). The full name + date range is
                       exposed as a native <code>title=</code> tooltip
                       on the input so the user can hover for the
                       complete context without the row overflowing. *@
                    <FluentTextField Value="@ActivePeriodText"
                                     ReadOnly="true"
                                     Title="@ActivePeriodTooltip"
                                     class="enroll-form-input--readonly" />
                </FormRow>

                <FormRow Label="Grade level" Required>
                    @* ONE shared grade picker for BOTH feature-flag paths: a
                       <CodedValueDropdown> over the GRADE coded values (with
                       per-tenant override names). The submit travels as the
                       picked CodedValueId; the CodedValueId -> GradeLevelId
                       join, auto-materialize of missing rows, and blocked-
                       from-enrollment enforcement all happen server-side in
                       <EnrollStudentHandler>.

                       The <FeatureFlagGate> now gates ONLY the inline-setup
                       buttons (they have global side-effects — new coded
                       value / rename of shared coded value — and are
                       therefore governance-gated):
                         - "+": inline-create-grade, ANDed with the
                           <IsNewEnrollment> check (re-enrollments pick an
                           existing grade rather than standing up a new one).
                         - "Override name": per-tenant rename of the SELECTED
                           grade; shown whenever the flag is on AND a grade is
                           picked.

                       The gate owns the flag entirely (it injects
                       <IFeatureFlagService> + the change notifier itself);
                       the dialog does NOT inject the flag service. *@
                    <div class="enroll-grade-row">
                        <CodedValueDropdown @ref="_gradeCodedValueDropdown"
                                            Parent="CodedValueParent.Grades"
                                            @bind-SelectedId="_formModel.GradeCodedValueId"
                                            @bind-SelectedId:after="OnGradePicked"
                                            Placeholder="Select a grade"
                                            class="enroll-grade-select" />
                        <FeatureFlagGate Key="@FeatureFlagKeys.EnableGradeLevelSetupOnEnrollDialog">
                            <ChildContent>
                                @* The "+" inline-create-grade button is gated by BOTH
                                   the new-enrollment check AND the runtime feature
                                   flag, ANDed together:
                                     1. <IsNewEnrollment> — the student being
                                        enrolled has no active enrollment yet. The
                                        Detail.razor / Edit.razor call sites pass
                                        the student's current active-enrollment
                                        grade as Model.SuggestedGradeLevelId; a
                                        null value means "no active enrollment",
                                        i.e. this is a new-enrollment scenario.
                                        For a re-enrollment (the student is already
                                        enrolled in a grade) the button is hidden
                                        because the right action is "pick a
                                        different existing grade" rather than
                                        "stand a brand-new grade up".
                                     2. FEATURE:EnableGradeLevelSetupOnEnrollDialog
                                        (opt-in via the ConfigFlags landing page,
                                        default false) — governance gate for the
                                        global side-effect (a new GRADE coded
                                        value; its GradeLevel row materializes
                                        server-side at enroll time).

                                   The two gates are ANDed because they cover
                                   different concerns: the new-enrollment check
                                   covers "is this the right time to offer
                                   grade setup" (UX correctness); the feature
                                   flag covers "is the tenant authorized to use
                                   inline grade setup at all" (governance).
                                   Either gate being false hides the button. *@
                                @if (IsNewEnrollment)
                                {
                                    <FluentButton Appearance="Appearance.Neutral"
                                                  Title="Create a new grade level for this tenant"
                                                  OnClick="OnAddNewGradeAsync"
                                                  Disabled="@_creatingGrade"
                                                  IconStart="@FluentIcons.Add"
                                                  class="enroll-grade-add" />
                                }
                                @* The "Override name" button renames the SELECTED grade
                                   per-tenant (mirrors the GradeLevelWizard's Override Name
                                   action). Shown when grade-level setup is allowed (the
                                   flag) AND a grade is picked — renaming an existing grade
                                   is valid for both new + re-enrollment (unlike the +
                                   create button, which is new-enrollment-only). On success
                                   the dropdown is refreshed so the per-tenant name shows
                                   immediately. *@
                                @if (_formModel.GradeCodedValueId is not null)
                                {
                                    <FluentButton Appearance="Appearance.Neutral"
                                                  Title="Override the selected grade's name for this tenant"
                                                  OnClick="OnOverrideGradeNameAsync"
                                                  Disabled="@_overridingGrade"
                                                  IconStart="@FluentIcons.Edit"
                                                  class="enroll-grade-override" />
                                }
                            </ChildContent>
                        </FeatureFlagGate>
                    </div>
                </FormRow>

                @* Grade stream picker. Filtered by the selected grade's
                   CodedValueId so it shows only streams whose gradeLevel
                   attribute matches the chosen grade. GUARD: the picker is
                   only RENDERED once a concrete (non-empty) grade coded
                   value is selected — with no grade there is no valid
                   filter, so we never issue a stream lookup at all (the
                   unfiltered GRSTREAMS list would show streams from every
                   grade). Until then a read-only placeholder row shows
                   instead. Uses the standard CodedValueDropdown augmented
                   with an attribute filter (key=gradeLevel,
                   value=selectedGradeCodedValueId). *@
                <FormRow Label="Stream" For="enroll-stream">

                    @if (GradeCodedValueIdForFilter is { } gradeFilterId)
                    {
                        <CodedValueDropdown Parent="CodedValueParent.Streams"
                                            AttributeFilter="@(("gradeLevel", gradeFilterId.ToString()))"
                                            EmptyFilterPlaceholder="No streams for this grade"
                                            ShowEmptyOption="true"
                                            EmptyOptionText="No stream"
                                            Placeholder="Select stream…"
                                            @bind-SelectedId="_formModel.StreamCodedValueId" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <FluentLabel>Select a grade first</FluentLabel>
                    }
                </FormRow>

                <FormRow Label="Enrolled on" Required>
                    @* FluentDatePicker binds to DateTime?; we convert
                       from the model's DateOnly? on the way in and back
                       on the way out. The input has no built-in label
                       (the FormRow above provides it). *@
                    <FluentDatePicker Value="@EnrolledOnAsDateTime"
                                      ValueChanged="@OnEnrolledOnChanged"
                                      class="enroll-form-input--enrolled-on" />
                    @* Per-field error display. Mirrors the dialog's
                       <Error> property (set by <SubmitAsync> on the
                       null-return or throw path) directly below the
                       date picker so the failure is visually adjacent
                       to the field that triggered it — a rejected
                       enrollment is almost always a date / grade /
                       period issue, and the date is the most user-
                       edited field on this form. The footer also
                       surfaces the same error (kept for symmetry
                       with every other <DialogShellBase> dialog);
                       this in-context display is the primary
                       user-facing message. *@
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Error))
                    {
                        <FluentMessageBar Intent="MessageIntent.Error"
                                          class="enroll-form-field-error">
                            @Error
                        </FluentMessageBar>
                    }
                </FormRow>
            </FluentStack>

            <DialogShellFooter Saving="@Saving"
                               Error="@Error"
                               SubmitText="Enroll"
                               SavingText="Enrolling…"
                               OnCancel="HandleCancelAsync" />
        </EditForm>
    }
</div>

@code {
    private readonly EnrollStudentFormModel _formModel = new();

    // Bridge: FluentDatePicker binds to DateTime?; the form model keeps the
    // API contract type (DateOnly?) and we convert on the way in and out.
    private DateTime? EnrolledOnAsDateTime => _formModel.EnrolledOn.HasValue
        ? _formModel.EnrolledOn.Value.ToDateTime(TimeOnly.MinValue)
        : null;

    private Task OnEnrolledOnChanged(DateTime? value)
    {
        _formModel.EnrolledOn = value.HasValue
            ? DateOnly.FromDateTime(value.Value)
            : null;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private bool _loading = true;
    private bool _creatingGrade;
    private bool _overridingGrade;

    /// <summary>Whether this dialog invocation is for a NEW enrollment
    /// (the student being enrolled has no active enrollment yet) versus
    /// a re-enrollment (the student is already enrolled in a grade and
    /// is being moved / re-enrolled in a different period or grade).
    /// Driven by <see cref="EnrollStudentModel.SuggestedGradeLevelId"/>:
    /// the call sites (Detail.razor / Edit.razor) pass the student's
    /// current active-enrollment grade as the suggested value, so a
    /// null value means "the student has no active enrollment". This
    /// is the validation check that gates inline grade-level setup
    /// inside the enrollment dialog: the "+" button next to the grade
    /// dropdown only renders when <c>IsNewEnrollment</c> is true. For
    /// a re-enrollment the button is hidden because the right action
    /// is "pick a different existing grade for the next term" rather
    /// than "stand a brand-new grade up mid-flow" — inline grade
    /// setup is appropriate only for the first-time-enrollment case
    /// (where the tenant has no grade configured yet AND is enrolling
    /// a student for the first time). The check is ANDed with the
    /// <c>FEATURE:EnableGradeLevelSetupOnEnrollDialog</c> feature
    /// flag, so the button is shown only when BOTH <c>IsNewEnrollment</c>
    /// is true AND the tenant has opted in to the inline setup path.</summary>
    private bool IsNewEnrollment => Model.SuggestedGradeLevelId is null;

    /// <summary>The tenant's current global period (Status == "Active").
    /// Derived client-side from <see cref="StudentsApiClient.ListPeriodsAsync"/>
    /// (same approach the <c>ActiveTermToolbar</c> uses). The server's
    /// <c>EnrollStudentHandler</c> enforces this same invariant via
    /// <c>IActivePeriodProvider.GetActivePeriodAsync()</c> and rejects
    /// any enrollment whose PeriodId does not match. The dialog's UI
    /// is read-only against this value — there is no period picker
    /// because the only valid enrollment period is the active one.</summary>
    private PeriodDto? _activePeriod;

    /// <summary>Read-only display string for the Period FormRow. Uses
    /// the canonical academic-year format
    /// <c>"{StartDate.Year}/{EndDate.Year}"</c> (e.g. <c>"2025/2026"</c>)
    /// so the read-only input cell always fits the full text on one
    /// line regardless of the period's name. The full name + date
    /// range is exposed as a native <c>title=</c> tooltip via
    /// <see cref="ActivePeriodTooltip"/> so the user can hover for
    /// the complete context.</summary>
    private string? ActivePeriodText => _activePeriod is { } p
        ? $"{p.StartDate.Year}/{p.EndDate.Year}"
        : null;

    /// <summary>Full-context tooltip for the Period FormRow. Combines
    /// the period's name with its date range (the same "Name (start –
    /// end)" formatting the original dropdown used to render) so a
    /// user hovering the field sees the complete context, not just
    /// the short academic-year token.</summary>
    private string? ActivePeriodTooltip => _activePeriod is { } p
        ? $"{p.Name} ({p.StartDate:yyyy-MM-dd} – {p.EndDate:yyyy-MM-dd})"
        : null;

    /// <summary>The CodedValueId selected in the grade <see cref="CodedValueDropdown"/>.
    /// Bound two-way to the dropdown (the dropdown's native id field) via
    /// <see cref="EnrollStudentFormModel.GradeCodedValueId"/> on the form model.
    /// Resolved to a <see cref="GradeLevelDto"/> via
    /// <see cref="OnGradeCodedValueChanged"/> for the actual enroll
    /// submission.</summary>
    // (field lives on _formModel.GradeCodedValueId)

    /// <summary>Reference to the grade <see cref="CodedValueDropdown"/>.
    /// The "+" inline-create-grade button calls
    /// <see cref="CodedValueDropdown.RefreshAsync"/> after creating a
    /// new grade so the new entry appears in the dropdown without a
    /// page reload.</summary>
    private CodedValueDropdown? _gradeCodedValueDropdown;

    // Stream selection lives on _formModel.StreamCodedValueId.

    /// <summary>Side-effect of a USER grade pick (fires via
    /// <c>@bind-SelectedId:after</c>, i.e. only when the dropdown itself raises
    /// <c>SelectedIdChanged</c> — never during the initial pre-selection of the
    /// student's current enrollment values). A stream belongs to exactly one
    /// grade (the picker is attribute-filtered by the selected grade's coded
    /// value), so switching grades invalidates any previously picked/streamed-in
    /// value — same rule as <c>StudentTransferDialog.OnGradeSelectedValueChanged</c>.
    /// Without this, a grade change followed by submit would send the OLD
    /// grade's stream id with the NEW grade.</summary>
    private Task OnGradePicked()
    {
        _formModel.StreamCodedValueId = null;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>The coded value id of the selected grade, used as the
    /// stream picker's <c>AttributeFilter</c> value. Null when no grade is
    /// selected yet OR the id is empty (the dropdown's sentinel) — the
    /// stream picker is not rendered at all in that case, so no stream
    /// lookup is ever issued without a concrete grade.</summary>
    private Guid? GradeCodedValueIdForFilter
    {
        get
        {
            var id = _formModel.GradeCodedValueId;
            return id is { } value && value != Guid.Empty ? value : null;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Selection state for the flag-OFF GradeLevel dropdown (the
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            // Load periods (to derive the active one). No student load - the
            // dialog intentionally does NOT render a "Student" row (the caller
            // already shows the student context on the page; re-stating it
            // here would be redundant). The grade <CodedValueDropdown> loads
            // its own GRADE coded values internally (via the shared widget's
            // GetChildrenByParentCodeAsync call) - no grade-level list load.
            var periods = await Api.ListPeriodsAsync(CancellationToken.None)
                ?? Array.Empty<PeriodDto>();
            // The current global period = the single period with
            // Status == "Active". The "at most one Active per tenant"
            // invariant is enforced by the server's Period domain +
            // activation flow (see PeriodRoutes). If a tenant ever
            // has more than one (data drift), we fall back to the
            // first match - the server is still the final authority.
            _activePeriod = periods.FirstOrDefault(p =>
                string.Equals(p.Status, "Active", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));

            // Pre-select the grade + stream the caller suggested (the student's
            // current active-enrollment values, if any). The grade suggestion is a
            // GradeLevel row id; resolve its coded value with a single-item
            // fetch (best-effort - an unknown/deleted grade just leaves the
            // picker empty) so the dropdown shows it pre-picked. The stream is
            // applied together with the grade because the stream picker is
            // attribute-filtered by the resolved grade's coded value — applying
            // a stream without its grade would leave it filtered to a different
            // grade and silently drop the pre-selection.
            if (Model.SuggestedGradeLevelId is { } suggestedId)
            {
                var suggestedGrade = await Api.GetGradeLevelByIdAsync(suggestedId, CancellationToken.None);
                if (suggestedGrade is null)
                {
                    Logger.LogWarning(
                        "Suggested grade level {GradeLevelId} for student {StudentId} no longer exists; leaving the grade picker empty",
                        suggestedId, Model.StudentId);
                }
                _formModel.LoadFrom(suggestedGrade, Model.SuggestedStreamCodedValueId);
            }
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // Task.WhenAll wraps failures in AggregateException. The
            // useful HTTP detail (status code + response body from
            // the manual error handling in StudentsApiClient) lives on
            // the INNER exception, so unwrap it before logging and
            // surfacing. Without this, the dialog shows only the
            // generic "One or more errors occurred." text.
            var root = ex is AggregateException agg
                ? agg.Flatten().InnerExceptions.FirstOrDefault() ?? ex
                : ex;
            Logger.LogError(root, "Failed to load enroll data for student {StudentId}", Model.StudentId);
            Error = root.Message;
        }
        finally
        {
            _loading = false;
        }
    }

    protected override async Task<EnrollStudentResult?> SubmitAsync(EnrollStudentModel model)
    {
        // Guard each required field with a specific, actionable error. The
        // EditForm has no DataAnnotationsValidator (the form model's fields
        // are guarded here so the messaging stays actionable per field), so
        // Blazor validation does NOT block submit when the grade is unset. Without
        // these guards a missing grade/period/date would silently return null
        // — HandleSubmitAsync would neither close the dialog nor set an error,
        // which presents to the user as "clicking Enroll does nothing". Surfacing
        // the cause as <Error> turns the silent no-op into a visible, actionable
        // message bar (rendered below the Enrolled-on field AND in the footer).
        if (_activePeriod is null)
        {
            Error = "No active academic period is open for this tenant. Open a period on the periods page before enrolling.";
            return null;
        }
        if (_formModel.GradeCodedValueId is null)
        {
            Error = "Select a grade level before enrolling.";
            return null;
        }
        // Grade resolution (CodedValueId -> GradeLevelId), auto-materialize of
        // missing rows, and blocked-from-enrollment enforcement are all
        // server-side now (EnrollStudentHandler) - the dialog just submits the
        // picked coded value id.
        if (_formModel.EnrolledOn is null)
        {
            Error = "Pick an enrolled-on date before enrolling.";
            return null;
        }

        try
        {
            await Api.EnrollStudentAsync(_formModel.ToEnrollRequest(
                model.StudentId,
                _activePeriod.Id));
            return new EnrollStudentResult(true);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // Surface the FULL tracing detail in the dialog's error
            // property. The per-field error MessageBar (rendered
            // directly below the Enrolled on date picker) AND the
            // shared DialogShellFooter both consume <Error> and
            // display the text; the user can read the full message
            // to understand WHAT went wrong (e.g. "EnrollStudent
            // failed (400 Bad Request): Cannot enrol students: no
            // active period is open for this tenant..."). We also
            // log the exception with its stack trace so the operator
            // can correlate the user's error with a server-side log
            // entry. The two together — user-facing message in the
            // bar + operator-facing stack in the log — give a
            // complete tracing path.
            Logger.LogError(ex, "Failed to enroll student {StudentId} in period {PeriodId} for grade coded value {GradeCodedValueId}",
                model.StudentId, _activePeriod.Id, _formModel.GradeCodedValueId);
            Error = ex.Message;
            return null;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Opens the shared <see cref="CodedValueDialog"/> in Create mode for
    /// the GRADE parent. On success the <see cref="CodedValueDropdown"/> is
    /// refreshed (so the new entry shows up) and the new grade is pre-selected
    /// so the user can immediately click Enroll. The matching GradeLevel row
    /// materializes server-side at enroll time (EnrollStudentHandler). A null
    /// result (user cancelled) is a no-op.
    /// <para>The <see cref="CodedValueDialog"/> in Create mode collects a
    /// Code, Name, DisplayOrder, and Description. The Name field is the
    /// <b>per-tenant override name</b>: the user can leave it empty to
    /// use the code as the display name, or enter a tenant-specific
    /// label (e.g. "Year 7" instead of "Grade 7" for a school that
    /// uses a different vocabulary).</para>
    /// <para>The button is disabled while a create is in flight to prevent
    /// double-clicks opening two dialogs. On any failure the dialog stays
    /// open with the error surfaced through the dialog's standard error
    /// path; the user can retry.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private async Task OnAddNewGradeAsync()
    {
        if (_creatingGrade) return;
        _creatingGrade = true;
        try
        {
            // Open the CodedValueDialog in Create mode for GRADE. The dialog
            // owns its own validation + save flow; on success it returns the
            // freshly created CodedValueDto (with the tenant-resolved name).
            var cvResult = await DialogService.ShowShellDialogAsync<CodedValueDialog, CodedValueFormModel, CodedValueDto>(
                CodedValueFormModel.ForCreate(parentId: null),
                title: "New grade",
                size: DialogSize.Medium);
            if (cvResult is null) return;

            // Refresh the dropdown so the new coded value is selectable, then
            // pre-select it. Its GradeLevel row materializes server-side when
            // the enrollment is submitted (EnrollStudentHandler).
            if (_gradeCodedValueDropdown is not null)
            {
                await _gradeCodedValueDropdown.RefreshAsync();
            }
            _formModel.GradeCodedValueId = cvResult.Id;
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            Logger.LogError(ex, "Failed to create grade level inline");
            Error = ex.Message;
        }
        finally
        {
            _creatingGrade = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Opens the shared <see cref="CodedValueDialog"/> in Override mode for the
    /// currently-selected grade, letting the tenant rename it per-tenant (e.g.
    /// "Grade 7" -> "Year 7"). Mirrors the GradeLevelWizard's "Override Name"
    /// action. Shown when grade-level setup is allowed (the flag) and a grade
    /// is picked. On success the <see cref="CodedValueDropdown"/> is refreshed
    /// so the per-tenant name shows immediately; the selected CodedValueId is
    /// unchanged so the user's selection is preserved. A null result (user
    /// cancelled) is a no-op.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task OnOverrideGradeNameAsync()
    {
        if (_overridingGrade) return;
        if (_formModel.GradeCodedValueId is null) return;
        var cvId = _formModel.GradeCodedValueId.Value;
        if (_gradeCodedValueDropdown is null
            || !_gradeCodedValueDropdown.TryFindItem(cvId, out var cv))
        {
            return;
        }
        if (cv is null) return;

        _overridingGrade = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await DialogService.ShowShellDialogAsync<CodedValueDialog, CodedValueFormModel, CodedValueDto>(
                CodedValueFormModel.ForOverride(cv, cv.IsOverridden),
                title: "Override grade name",
                size: DialogSize.Medium);
            if (result is null) return;

            // Refresh the dropdown so the overridden (per-tenant) name shows
            // immediately. The selected CodedValueId is unchanged so the
            // user's selection is preserved.
            await _gradeCodedValueDropdown.RefreshAsync();
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            Logger.LogError(ex, "Failed to override grade name for coded value {CodedValueId}", cvId);
            Error = ex.Message;
        }
        finally
        {
            _overridingGrade = false;
        }
    }
}
